# Copy this file to .env.local and restart `npm run dev` only when the
# defaults below do not describe your machine. Nothing here is a secret.

# Where the browser sends API calls. The default is a relative path, which
# next.config.ts forwards to the backend - that keeps one origin and avoids
# cross-origin rules entirely.
#
# Set it to a full address instead when you want the browser to talk to the
# API directly (then the backend's CORS_ORIGINS must list this frontend).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# The backend's real address, used by the rewrite above. Change it if uvicorn
# runs elsewhere: a different port, another machine, a phone on the same wifi.
#
# A phone cannot reach "localhost", so use the machine's LAN address:
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://192.168.1.20:8000
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8000
